% =============================================================================
% rill — reactive ILL: fill + the ○ next-time modality (TODO_0203, THY_0042)
% =============================================================================
%
% rill = fill (ILL + μ/ν fixed points) + ○ (next tick). It is the FRP / temporal
% layer — signals νX.(A & ○X), streams μX.(A ⊕ ○X) — forked out of fill so the
% soundness-subtle temporal machinery is firewalled from fill's now-audited μMALL
% core, exactly as fill firewalls μMALL from production ILL. fill declares no ○,
% so nothing below reaches the μ/ν calculus or ILL's EVM proof path.
%
% @extends fill → the meta-parser merges fill's chain (ILL's connectives + mu/nu)
% and rill adds ONLY the ○ modality below.

@extends fill.

% =============================================================================
% Temporal modality
% =============================================================================

% Next-time: ○A — "A is available at the NEXT tick, not now."
%
% Polarity: positive (a delayed value; its right rule is a focusing constructor,
% promotion-shaped). There is deliberately NO left/elimination rule — an ○A can
% never be consumed in the present, so ○ does not collapse: ○a ⊬ a and a ⊬ ○a.
% @category modality is a FRESH category (deriveRoles assigns it no engine role),
% so the cyclic-proof engine is untouched: for a guarded signal νX.(A & ○X) the
% ν-unfold already discharges the GTC progress condition, and ○ is the syntactic
% guard, not a trace-participating step.
circle: formula -> formula
  @ascii "O #1"
  @latex "\\bigcirc #1"
  @prec 85
  @category modality
  @polarity positive.
